      "state": "open",
      "changedFiles": 9,
      "issue": 28,
      "bodyHtml": "<h2>What this does</h2><p>Adds a shadow-mode spike that asks Jev which view fits each shopper request, and logs its pick next to the view we show today. Shoppers see no change.</p><h2>Rollout plan</h2><ol><li>Run in shadow mode for a week and compare picks.</li><li>Split the React rendering into three smaller PRs.</li><li>Do the owner-only Shopify content tasks first, since the cards depend on them.</li></ol><h2>Checklist</h2><ul class=\"contains-task-list\"><li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" disabled checked> Unit tests for the picker</li><li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" disabled checked> Eval on 40 recorded shopper requests</li><li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" disabled> Your sign-off on the rollout order</li></ul><h2>Eval results</h2><table><thead><tr><th>View</th><th>Jev picked</th><th>Matched today</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Grid</td><td>18</td><td>15</td></tr><tr><td>Gift picks</td><td>9</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>Comparison</td><td>8</td><td>5</td></tr></tbody></table><h2>Try it</h2><p>Set <code>JEV_SHADOW</code> and watch the log:</p><pre><code>JEV_SHADOW=1 npm run dev\n# picks land in logs/jev-shadow.ndjson</code></pre><blockquote><p>The run chose shadow mode because it can be reversed with one flag (decision 0023).</p></blockquote>",
